  "Question": "For distinct real numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y,\\) let \\(M(x,y)\\) be the larger of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) and let \\(m(x,y)\\) be the smaller of \\(x\\) and \\(y.\\) If \\[ a\\lt b\\lt c\\lt d\\lt e, \\] then \\[ \\begin{aligned} &M\\bigl(M(a,m(b,c)),\\\\ &\\qquad m(d,m(a,e))\\bigr)= \\end{aligned} \\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(a\\)",
    "B": "\\(b\\)",
    "C": "\\(c\\)",
    "D": "\\(d\\)",
    "E": "\\(e\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Use the given order to evaluate the innermost selections first. Since \\(b<c\\) and \\(a<e\\),\n\\[\nm(b,c)=b,\\qquad m(a,e)=a.\n\\]\nThe two arguments of the outer \\(M\\) therefore become\n\\[\nM(a,b)=b,\\qquad m(d,a)=a.\n\\]\nFinally, since \\(a<b\\), the whole expression is \\(M(b,a)=b\\). All compared arguments are distinct, as required by the definitions. The answer is \\(\\boxed{b}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
